From 7e61b3c90784083e4d99b6203d57203802caf1e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mattia D'Oronzo <doronzomattia26@icloud.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 16:37:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 04/13] usb: typec: Type-C class, TCPM and FUSB302 from Linux
 4.16, with the HiBy board data

The R3 Pro II has a FUSB302B on the CC lines, registered by the stock
fusb302b_add module with a struct fusb302_platform_data. Taken from 4.16
(the version the vendor kernel matches), plus what the vendor added:

- board data: sink limits, the charger to follow and the OTG ID GPIO;
- the charger is told the power role (TYPEC_POWER_ROLE) and when to
  source VBUS (USB_OTG);
- the ID GPIO gives the USB controller its data role;
- a "power" regulator kept on while bound;
- no extcon: no BC1.2 detection is wired to the chip.
